Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: brightness ramps with the colour fade off

DisplayPowerController skips the brightness ramp while "the display content
is not visible", which it defines as the colour fade being enabled and
fully faded in. This phone disables the colour fade
(config_displayColorFadeDisabled, no fade animation on e-ink), so that test
is false forever and every brightness change, automatic or not, is applied
in one frame. The slow ramp rate (kompakt_brightness.xml) and 0164 could
never run; the kernel log showed L:87 then L:31 with nothing between.

With the colour fade off the content is always visible, so the test reads
that way, and the automatic brightness walks the ramp: a change of room
fades through every number between two rows.
---
 .../com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java  | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/DisplayPowerController.java
@@ -1698,8 +1698,10 @@
                     Display.isDozeState(state) && mBrightnessBucketsInDozeConfig;
             // If the color fade is totally covering the screen then we can change the backlight
             // level without it being a noticeable jump since any actual content isn't yet visible.
+            // Kompakt: with the colour fade off (config_displayColorFadeDisabled) the content is
+            // always visible; stock read "off" as "never visible" and skipped every ramp.
             final boolean isDisplayContentVisible =
-                    mColorFadeEnabled && mPowerState.getColorFadeLevel() == 1.0f;
+                    !mColorFadeEnabled || mPowerState.getColorFadeLevel() == 1.0f;
             // We only want to animate the brightness if it is between 0.0f and 1.0f.
             // brightnessState can contain the values -1.0f and NaN, which we do not want to
             // animate to. To avoid this, we check the value first.
